gory'. I can use 'filter_pages_by_content_type' on the current page again, but since it returned no categories earlier, I need to explore other pages. Let me use 'explore_page_and_links' on the current page to find linked pages, then for each linked page, quickly check if it has 'health' in its URL or title. This might be simpler. I'll call 'explore_page_and_links' with start_url as the current page's relative URL ('/?page_id=2'). This will return a list of pages linked from the Sample Page. I can then search through those pages for 'health' in the URL or title. Once found, I can navigate to that URL. This approach uses an available function and should complete the task. I'll write code to call 'explore_page_and_links', print the result as-is, then iterate through the pages to find one with 'health' in the title or URL. If found, navigate to it. If not, I might need to explore further, but I'll assume it will be found.",
